From: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 10:39:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-eip: restore PPE outer-inline IPsec on Linux 6.18

Use the 6.18 qcom PPE API to steer inbound ESP and NAT-T flows from the
physical ingress port through EIP-197 and return decrypted packets through
a per-SA virtual port.  Keep host lookaside as a per-SA fallback when
routing, PPE, EIP flow, or VP resources are unavailable.

Allocate separate lookaside and hybrid contexts, direct hybrid
decapsulation records to the EIP inline interface, and share four DMA IRQs
between eight rings according to each ring's RX CPU.  Quiesce PPE, EIP,
RCU, and NAPI users in teardown order before invalidating a transform
record.

Fully inline packets do not run a host completion callback.  Periodically
consume transform-record packet and byte deltas to maintain driver and
XFRM lifetime accounting, and take a final snapshot after stopping the
hardware flows.  Exception punts only record the VP miss so those packets
are not counted twice.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/169bf594df03ac4b29e0ccd3f6f87e70f0f3fb6e
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/39c0281b98922dcda04f91e30dd15bccbb0896ae
Signed-off-by: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Tushar Ganatra <tganatra@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
